   "Statement": "<b>Occupation<br></b>Attorney and PT Judge; UW Law Adjunct Professor; Board Member; Former Full-Time Judge and Court Commissioner&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"><b>Education<br></b>UW Tacoma and UW School of Law&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"><b>Statement<br></b>I believe our judiciary must reflect the values of the community it serves. That conviction — backed by a proven record on the bench — is why I am running for Pierce County District Court Judge. </p><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">My career in private practice, public defense, and the judiciary gives me a well-rounded courtroom perspective. I have served as a Municipal Court Judge, &nbsp;Superior Court Commissioner, and Judge Pro Tem. I know how to run a courtroom that is fair, efficient, and accessible. My commitment to service has been recognized with the DMCJA Presidential Award and UW Tacoma’s Celebrando Communidad Award for Social Justice. </p><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Tacoma is the first place I called home in this country.&nbsp; Pierce County helped shape who I am, and I am ready to bring my experience back to serve the community that gave me so much. I am honored to be endorsed by judicial officers and community leaders throughout Washington.&nbsp;</p><p> </p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">",
